{"from": "passage:lk-23-11", "type": "related_to", "to": "passage:mt-27-27", "note": "related_to rather than parallels: Luke 23:11 is Herod's soldiers dressing Jesus in luxurious clothing at Herod's house; Matthew 27:27 and Mark 15:16 are Pilate's soldiers dressing him in a scarlet/purple robe after the flogging at the Praetorium. Different soldiers, place and clothing - a shared soldiers'-mockery motif in two different scenes (the jn-19-02 precedent). Converted per the architect's bundled-claims ruling (2026-11-15)."}
